    {
      "id": "xetra-newsboard-emergency-2020-07-01",
      "title": "Xetra & Frankfurt Newsboard: Emergency Information MIC: XETR, Update, Trading resumption (1 July 2020)",
      "publisher": "Deutsche Börse AG",
      "location": "https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/cash-en/Stay-Informed/newsroom/Xetra-Frankfurt-Newsboard/Emergency-Information-MIC-XETR-2090144 (update -2090372, resumption -2095186)",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "covers": "2020-07-01",
      "notes": "\"Due to problems the Xetra T7 is not available at the moment\"; restart with pre-trading not before 11:15 CEST and the auction call not before 11:45 CEST. The session completed with a normal close (Börsen-Zeitung: \"Der Dax schloss ... auf 12 261 Punkten\"). A delayed open, not a closure.",
      "local_files": [],
      "support_intervals": [
        {
          "scope": "UNSCHEDULED_EXCEPTIONS",
          "from": "2020-07-01",
          "to": "2020-07-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "xetra-newsboard-emergency-2020-04-14",
      "title": "Xetra & Frankfurt Newsboard: Emergency Information MIC: XETR (14 April 2020)",
      "publisher": "Deutsche Börse AG",
      "location": "https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/cash-en/Stay-Informed/newsroom/Xetra-Frankfurt-Newsboard/Emergency-Information-MIC-XETR-1932466",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "covers": "2020-04-14",
      "notes": "\"The technical problem in the Xetra market (MIC: XETR) is resolved.\" Trading halted from about 09:25 to 13:45 CEST and the closing auction ran (dpa: DAX 10,696.56 at 17:55). Reuters and the exchange called it one of the longest outages ever, which excludes any full-day closure in the system's history. An intraday halt, not a closure.",
      "local_files": [],
      "support_intervals": [
        {
          "scope": "UNSCHEDULED_EXCEPTIONS",
          "from": "2020-04-14",
          "to": "2020-04-14"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "xetra-newsboard-emergency-search",
      "title": "Xetra & Frankfurt Newsboard, every \"emergency\" item (2018-2026 retention)",
      "publisher": "Deutsche Börse AG",
      "location": "https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/cash-en/Stay-Informed/newsroom/Xetra-Frankfurt-Newsboard/4091644!search?query=emergency",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "covers": "2018-01-01 to 2026-09-30",
      "notes": "The exchange's own incident notices: besides the two 2020 items, every XETR notice (7 March 2024 FIX interface, 6 June 2024 matcher failover, 10 November 2025 partition 60 closing auction extended to 19:15 CET for some instruments, 21 November 2025 GUI) is partial, and the 29 October 2018 \"MARKET HALT\", 28 November 2025 and 31 August 2026 notices concern Börse Frankfurt (MIC XFRA), not Xetra. No notice records a whole-day closure or a market-wide early termination.",
